{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage","id":1223891,"title":"Creating an antagonistic Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-01T05:39:17-07:00","id":1223891,"title":"Creating an antagonistic Mage","content":"Hi all, I am the ST of a Werewolf game and the main antagonist of the campaign is a Mage. I would like your help in defining him. I didn't know if posting here or in the Werewolf forum but in the end you are the experts in Mages. If you feel this does not belong here just tell me and I will move it.<br /> <br /> I am currently reading the M20 book but it is dense and taking so damm long, by the time I've finished a chapter I seem to have forgotten what there was in the previous one.<br /> <br /> I know that I could just create a custom enemy with made up powers and call it a day, but it would feel like I'm cheating (maybe this is stupid) and my players may sense I am pulling things out of my ass, so while this guy does not have to have a character sheet I would like to make him as close to the Mage system as possible. And because they might encounter him before I have finished the book it seems logical to have something prepared, can you help me?<br /> <br /> I have a basic understanding of the system by reading this forum and some wiki pages + first chapters of the M20 book but if I butcher any term or concept please let me know.<br /> <br /> This guy, lets name him Steve, is at his core a specialist in spirits, he can cross the Gaunlet, pull people to and from the Umbra, command spirits and trap them (willingly or not) into objects e.g. Genie jars. His objective is thinning the Gaunlet which has put him at odds with the Garou as his experiments may use some (a lot) of kinfolk blood.<br /> He is not a flashy guy throwing fireballs or kinking people into the moon but he needs some kind of offense and defense, for offense he lets the spirits he has trapped deal with the problems and for defense I was thinking on some kind of wards, statics if they need to be with maybe some silver for dealing with Garous in particular.<br /> The wards won't last forever so in my mind he has the rote &quot;I will just use my secret exit&quot; which enables him to pull from a book in a bookshelf, lamp statue or any other object typically associated with secret doors and open a door which didn't exists before.<br /> He is also fond of using a projection to deal with other parties to avoid the possible risk to his health. This projection is incorporeal but looks solid to the sight.<br /> <br /> I want this mage to have the upper hand during the duration of the campaign, always being able to scape or just being 1 step further than my players but being beatable in some form (knowing my players, by killing him) when they have enough intel about him.<br /> <br /> My questions in the end are:<ul><li>Is there some kind of &quot;level&quot; system such as rank in Werewolf and generation in Vampire that allows me to say, a mage with this many sphere dots would be a &quot;archmage&quot; or at very least he is very well known in the country? I want him to be kind of obscure and not too powerful.</li> <li>For the spirits powers I describe, are they possible? and in case they are, how many dots does he need in the Spirit sphere?</li> <li>For the wardings I have no idea what to use.</li> <li>For the secret doors at first I thought Correspondence but you are moving matter so you need Matter and once you use Matter why would you need Correspondence?</li> <li>For the secrets door would it make it harder/easier and more/less vulgar if the door mechanism last or if someone that tries to replicate it cannot produce the same result?</li> <li>For the experiments with the kinfolk blood that in the end produce a consumable that can be eaten and used by sleepers, Matter again?</li> <li>For the projection power, Correspondence for the distance, Forces for the image and sound?, Matter if he wants to interact</li> <li>Do Garou count as witnesses for vulgar magic?</li> <li>From reading this forum and the book it seems that a mage in his &quot;Sanctum Sanctorum&quot; (chantries?) has his powers amplified and it is impervious to paradox backslashes. If my players walk into his house, are they done for?</li> </ul><br /> <br /> What I want is an enemy that feels consistent with the rules even if it deviates a little.<br /> <br /> PD: His paradigm is a mix of Vodou and Christianity, he believing that all his powers come from his ability to command Spirits, even the ones that are not affected by the Spirit sphere.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20067-hares666","name":"Hares666","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20067_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T07:23:43-07:00","id":1223905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage#post1223891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Is there some kind of &quot;level&quot; system such as rank in Werewolf and generation in Vampire that allows me to say, a mage with this many sphere dots would be a &quot;archmage&quot; or at very least he is very well known in the country? I want him to be kind of obscure and not too powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for you to understand the &quot;power level&quot; of mage you should take in consideration their Arete which is alone used on Magick rolls, however what truly defines what makes a character really powerfull isnt his &quot;magic muscle&quot;, but their Spheres dots, you see as you asked a character to be defined an Archmage must have on sphere in rank 6 - archmaestry. Even if you have a character with 6 or more arete it doest not count exactly as and archmage. But to define excessive strength you have to consider that mages are not battle oriented as werewolves are, and if they try do do so they may get underrated or absurdly overpower. Just an example: if Steve wants to throw a lighting bolt at &quot;pc 1&quot;, he rolls 3 successes, and he wants to put all those successes in damage, it will deal 2 damage per success and +1 for merely using Forces sphere, it will be in total 7 points of aggravated damage, because all damages done by Forces are naturally aggravated. Well Im happy for you that garou can soak agg, because if not, damn if it would be fatal damage done by a mere starting character with Forces 3 and Arete 3.<br /> However remember, what maks mages fking powerfull isnt Forces alone, but the absurd versatility those guys have, they can do EVERYTHING a garou and any other splat form world of darks can do, at the cost of paradox.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage#post1223891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]For the spirits powers I describe, are they possible? and in case they are, how many dots does he need in the Spirit sphere?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are quite possible and you dont need that much high ranks for such, you can do that about going in the umbra with Lvl 3, but to imprison spirits on objects against their will it needs to be 4, also about taking people here and there so easily also means 4, with this lvl you can rip the boundaries of the spirit and material world, literally opening a portal betwen the two. (knowing that how could malfean nephandi corrupted mages didnt just summon Wyrm on the fking world already is beyong me)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage#post1223891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]For the wardings I have no idea what to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends of what you understand by wards, in mage terms is to completely negate or difficult usage of said routine or sphere in all of its regards. If you're talking about defending oneself about, lets say, Paw of the Newborn-bla-bla-overrated-gift, all you would probably need is Spirit, Prime or other spheres you think to be, by logic, part of the intended purpose, like healing with Life, mind control with Mind, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage#post1223891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]For the secret doors at first I thought Correspondence but you are moving matter so you need Matter and once you use Matter why would you need Correspondence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it depends, I myself never use Correspondence as dependent of any other sphere to work by itself if the paradigm of said character doesnt imply such usage. Say, Steve wants to enter the shadows and teleport faraway, you dont need Life to do such, but if Steve wants to enter the Digital Web by making his body becomes data bites, yeah he will need Life.<br /> Oh and the level need is 3 for Correspondence alone, if another is used along they will need the same level at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage#post1223891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]For the secrets door would it make it harder/easier and more/less vulgar if the door mechanism last or if someone that tries to replicate it cannot produce the same result?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would only last if the intended purpose was to make it last, he just teleported or he actually made a portal which requires A LOT more successes? Frankly one would only make a portal if they REALLY wants to have this place connected with another to make time-usage faster.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage#post1223891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]For the experiments with the kinfolk blood that in the end produce a consumable that can be eaten and used by sleepers, Matter again?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont know, what ends you think you will get by using it, makes people a bit spirit? Makes them easier to be snatched into another dimension? You only use a Sphere if the Effect has parts of it directly related to the sphere usage, as much as the teleport example. Using blood makes a lot of sense, but we have to understand what exactly you want it to be used for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage#post1223891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]For the projection power, Correspondence for the distance, Forces for the image and sound?, Matter if he wants to interact</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends of how you want to do it, you may even use Mind alone for such. But matter actually makes them made of some matter, Forces can emulate physical stimulation, at high levels.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage#post1223891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Do Garou count as witnesses for vulgar magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, as much as mages doesnt count to delirium effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage#post1223891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]From reading this forum and the book it seems that a mage in his &quot;Sanctum Sanctorum&quot; (chantries?) has his powers amplified and it is impervious to paradox backslashes. If my players walk into his house, are they done for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the mages powers, being in a Sanctum does not make a mage more powerful than outside it, it merely takes away their restrictions, like Paradox, which would looks they are way more powerful since now they can actually use their power.[/LIST]<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage#post1223891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PD: His paradigm is a mix of Vodou and Christianity, he believing that all his powers come from his ability to command Spirits, even the ones that are not affected by the Spirit sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>About this, take in note that paradigm is the root of a mage's magick as much as it is the seed of their undoing<br /> I you cant let an Hermetic chant his spell the spell may not work, I think it would be fun for the players to learn how to understand the mages Paradigm and play it against her/him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","user":"menos125","date":". 06-01-2018, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T16:39:08-07:00","id":1224023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage#post1223891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Is there some kind of &quot;level&quot; system such as rank in Werewolf and generation in Vampire that allows me to say, a mage with this many sphere dots would be a &quot;archmage&quot; or at very least he is very well known in the country? I want him to be kind of obscure and not too powerful.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I began writing an extensive answer to this but then realised that you probably were not looking for a lecture, so; Archmages, according to Master's of the Art and if I recall correctly, need to have three things: Hubris (Because becoming an archmage is actually a bad thing), Renown, and a Sphere above 5. Judging from the Hermetics, a minimum archmage would have a Sphere of 6, and two Spheres at 3, although that sounds ridiculously small for an archmage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T19:32:16-07:00","id":1224049,"title":"","content":"Theme question: Vodou is already syncretized with Christianity. Is this just a case where there's an extra helping of Christianity?<br /> <br /> Mages can easily have non-magical cohorts such as a family, congregation, civic group, community and such that can fill in whatever holes you encounter. This also allows the Mage to have more firepower of whatever type you need without throwing in an extra dot. Mages also have access to chiminage to barter with spirits and, if doing work with Vodou, maybe even the undead so you have a lot of knobs to work with. Whether your character is a Houngan, a Mambo, or bokor, you have a lot of options for invoking powers from any of the main families augmented with the Christian saints either as a focus or through their spirit agents.<br /> <br /> Also, when you're throwing in another system, there's nothing to say can't just have a list of vague powers that you want to work with. The full system for Wraith is a bit daunting but thumbing through Arcanos gives you ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T21:48:36-07:00","id":1224080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage#post1223891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Is there some kind of &quot;level&quot; system such as rank in Werewolf and generation in Vampire that allows me to say, a mage with this many sphere dots would be a &quot;archmage&quot; or at very least he is very well known in the country? I want him to be kind of obscure and not too powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>menos125</b> answer covers the mechanical quirks that make a potent mage. I'm going to focus in the social/metaplot aspect of your question, that has also a mechanical component: Mages, roughly, identify themselves by the level of mastery reached in one (probably several) Spheres. For instance:<br /> With one Sphere at 3 you're a Disciple of that Sphere. Disciple it's also a rank within the Traditions, directly above Apprentice and below Adept - it'sthe rank and file of mages. However inside of character nobody knows how many dots you have, all that people knows it's that you're capable of things, perhaps things that an Apprentice can't do.<br /> Now, I'm oversimplifying stuff here: each mage group has it's own rules about when a mage can be considered part of the rank and file. Somethimes it has little to do with Spheres or Arete (in the Technocracy being good at your job matters more among the lower ranks). Most groups of mages would require you to have more than one sphere at 3 to be regarded as a Disciple or equivalent, but lvl 3 it's a very common staple.<br /> <br /> When you reach 5 in a Sphere you're a Master. Again, no Master worthy of the title will have only one Sphere at 5, but having 5 it's mandatory - even in the Technocracy you can't be the big boss without one Sphere at 5. These mages are the ones that rule the world of mages, they have the potential of being very well known unless they have voluntarily choosen a life of anonimate.<br /> <br /> Now, for your character, judging for the things you want him to accomplish and the fact you don't want him to be too powerful I would suggest to make either an Adept or a Disciple with a powerful Mentor.<br /> <br /> As an Adept, Steeve it's a powerful mage but not so powerful as to be a luminary. It's the social equivalent of an Ancilla - big enough to take care for himself but he ain't going to become the Prince if there's a Master in town (so to speak, in truth Masters tend to live of world and Adepts are the most potent dudes you may find). He may have 12-20 points in Spheres without being too flashy. Arete 5 should be OK<br /> <br /> As a Disciple he would fill the bill of being &quot;obscure and not too powerful&quot;, but won't be able to do the stuff you want him to do because the effects you want require at least Spirit 4.<br /> However, a powerful Mentor may have provided Steve with Artifacts capable of doing the feat. Perhaps Steve's Mentor it's the one that suggested the experiments that Steve it's doing. Perhaps Steve's Mentor wants to lower the Gauntlet because perhaps he got traped in the Umbra during the Avatar Storm, and now he needs a hole in the Gauntlet to pass safely. Or perhaps he has other reasons.<br /> The advantage of this route it's that you have more stories to tell (what will Steve's Mentor do when he notices his apprentice has been ripped apart?). The disadvantage it's that a pack of Garou may be more than what Steve can handle - but if you're going with the assumption that Steve it's very inteligent and resourcefull, he may be able to do the job. For this build, I would recommend someone slightly more powerful than chargen, perhaps with 9 points in Spheres and Arete 4<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This guy, lets name him Steve, is at his core a specialist in spirits, he can cross the Gaunlet, pull people to and from the Umbra, command spirits and trap them (willingly or not) into objects e.g. Genie jars.[*]For the spirits powers I describe, are they possible? and in case they are, how many dots does he need in the Spirit sphere? </div> </div> </div><b>menos125</b> nailed it, you need Spirit 4 for most of those effects.<br /> <br /> If you want to go with Disciple Steve, then he would need a level 4 Wonder - could easily be a Genie Jar - that traps spirits and allows to command them afterwards. You could make several &quot;one use&quot; genie jars that allow to capture spirits instead - these would also count as a 4 level Wonder. He would also need a Wonder to pull people from and to the Umbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]For the wardings I have no idea what to use. </div> </div> </div>Wards that block passage are the ones that would hinder Garou the most (because they so love to sharpen their claws on other people's faces). A Correspondence 4/Spirit 2/Life 1 Ward can prevent Garou from getting too close. Correspondence 4 creates a Major Ward, a distortion in space that prevents passage and can't be broken by pure brute force, while Spirit + Life are needed to detect Garou so the ward can block them, Spirit 2 it's for the ward to affect the Umbra.<br /> Such a Ward could protect a house (Garou can't enter the house), an item, or could be worn as an amulet by Steve (so he can't be atacked in mele with claws or theet, but swords or really any other weapon would be OK - as long as he hasn't wards against those)<br /> <br /> Disicple Steve hasn't access to such potent Wards, however he can manage. A Correspondence 2/Life 1/Spirit 2 Minnor Ward can alert Steve that Garou are entering his house. Add Mind 3 and the ward can cause potent feelings of &quot;don't enter this house, leave now&quot; (that can be resisted as any mental influence).<br /> <br /> Forces 2 can conjure forcefields, that may be all the ward you need. Unlike Correspondence Wards, enough brute force should be able to overpower a forcefield.<br /> In M20 you need Matter 2 if you want to put a forcefiled in a building or another material object without concentrating on the spell, if you don't want to use this whole &quot;pattern locking&quot; rules fell free to house-rule them away, nothing breaks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]From reading this forum and the book it seems that a mage in his &quot;Sanctum Sanctorum&quot; (chantries?) has his powers amplified and it is impervious to paradox backslashes. If my players walk into his house, are they done for? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]For the secret doors at first I thought Correspondence but you are moving matter so you need Matter and once you use Matter why would you need Correspondence? </div> </div> </div>You need Matter 4 to create a real secret door (one that can be opened by other people, at least theoretically) .<br /> <br /> You need Correspondence 3 when you are truly vanishing into thin air.<br /> <br /> It's worth to note that under M20 you can't &quot;conjure a secret door&quot; to make your magick Coincident using Correspondence (and to do so with Matter would require you to also craft the passageway, wich would require a ton of successes). Only 1rst edition allowed this kind of benefitial &quot;artistic licency&quot; when using magick (the in-famous conjured taxicab)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]For the secrets door would it make it harder/easier and more/less vulgar if the door mechanism last or if someone that tries to replicate it cannot produce the same result? </div> </div> </div>The axis of Coincidence it's determined at the moment of the casting - people trying to replicate your feat has no relevance, all that matters it's if what you did would be considered magical or impossible by a bystander.<br /> <br /> Note that teleportation it's almost always Vulgar, and it's supposed to be. A price that mages would pay gladly if it means to not confront the Garou. Vanishing behind a secret door...It's still, most likely, Vulgar (what if someone was in the secret passage?) - there may be ways to make this Coincident, but not without falling in edge cases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]For the experiments with the kinfolk blood that in the end produce a consumable that can be eaten and used by sleepers, Matter again? </div> </div> </div>As<b> menos125 </b>says, it depends...<br /> <br /> If you want it to have a magical effect, you're probably thinking in Prime. Prime 3 can enchant a substane into a consumables that causes magical effects, called Charms. Prime 2 it's enough if you use Tass with a ressonance appropiate to the spell the object it's going to cast - which you could rule kinfolk blood it's (this would be a house rule - kinfolk usually don't count as magical creatures, albeit kinfolk with Gnosis could be the exception). Note that the mage needs to be able to cast the spell he's imbuing into the charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]For the projection power, Correspondence for the distance, Forces for the image and sound?, Matter if he wants to interact </div> </div> </div>Correspondence 2/Forces 2 it's enough. Forces can't just project light and sound, but also Kinetic force - you can touch stuff with it. It's higly Vulgar, but also beats having Garou sharpening their claws in your back. Note that with Corr 3 you can also cast spells where your projection is, and with Corr 2/Matter 2 you could teleport small stuff there (like, say, a grenade)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]Do Garou count as witnesses for vulgar magic? </div> </div> </div>Never, ever.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk count as witnesses, but only if they aren't so jaded by their experience with garou as to wholeheartedly believe in anything supernatural<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From reading this forum and the book it seems that a mage in his &quot;Sanctum Sanctorum&quot; (chantries?) has his powers amplified and it is impervious to paradox backslashes. If my players walk into his house, are they done for? </div> </div> </div>Not quite.<br /> <br /> See, a Sanctum doesn't make you immune to Paradox, it makes your magick Coincident as long as it stays there. Thus, you can't get Paradox unless you Botch and the difficulty it's reduced so you can get more successes. But if your magick was already Coincident, casting it in a sanctum hasn't much benefit. Also if you, say, want to teleport outside the Sanctum to escape, it's Vulgar (unless you teleport into ANOTHER Sanctum).<br /> But you still have to roll.<br /> A fireball casted by an Arete 3 mage within a Sanctum it's still going to cause a maximum of 8 (10 if Willpower it's expended) levels of aggravated damage, the only advantage it's that getting the maximum amount of successes it's going to be easier and you won't get 'dox.<br /> <br /> The real danger of the Sanctum for Garou it's the amount of milacres Steve may have stored there without fear of Paradox. Vulgar traps and items are very common in Sanctums, since you don't have to worry about them being crushed by reality. However, again, that depends on Steve's capabilities - a Disciple ain't likely to have a dragon in his Sanctum. Since Steve it's a Spirit mage, he could have a bound guardian spirit<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> PD: His paradigm is a mix of Vodou and Christianity, he believing that all his powers come from his ability to command Spirits, even the ones that are not affected by the Spirit sphere. </div> </div> </div>Maybe you want to research about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santer%C3%ADa\" target=\"_blank\">Santeria</a>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-02-2018, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T00:44:42-07:00","id":1224103,"title":"","content":"With regards to a Sanctum; if a Garou enters the Sanctum of a powerful Mage, alone (assuming they can find it; they have an Arcane rating which shields them) they may be destroyed. However they have an advantage; the Sanctum does not impact their powers at all. If a rival Mage enters your sanctum, and their magick doesn't fit your practice, then they will struggle to use their powers. Garou will function as normal, just against a powerful enemy.<br /> <br /> The sanctum will likely have a very thin Gauntlet, so these Garou PCs might be able to enter through the Umbra. If I were this Mage I would have wards which detect inbound Spirits and Living Creatures (Spirit/Correspondence and Life/Correspondence).<br /> <br /> You should read the Fetish rules for Mages. A Mage with command over Spirits, who is pissing off Garou, could easily be forcing spirits into their instruments to gain power.<br /> <br /> I think the best way to make a Mage an interesting antagonist in another game is to tie them very closely to the splat. For example, a Mage NPC in a Vampire game could be a Revenant or Ghoul, or be a Hermetic who works for Clan Tremere, or a Lych of the True Black Hand. If this Mage were in some way linked to the Garou, by cosmology or bloodlines, then it would make their presence feel less random.<br /> <br /> Last of all, there's a Werewolf rite/gift (I believe) which commands Paradox Spirits. I think it's a Glass Walker / Werespider thing since it's weaver-related. Regardless, if a PC had the power to influence paradox spirits they could completely destroy this Mage with some good rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 06-02-2018, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T03:03:34-07:00","id":1224120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage#post1223891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]For the projection power, Correspondence for the distance, Forces for the image and sound?, Matter if he wants to interact<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Correspondence 4 can do this, it is called co-locate self. M20 Corebook says that Conjunctional Mind 1 is also needed.<br /> Conjunctional Life 2 is needed to make each of the co-located selves capable of independent action and interaction with what is at a given location ; otherwise the actions of the co-located selves will be the same as actions of the casting Mage.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 can project an image of the Mage ( without the possibility of interacting with other persons or the environment ) , this Effect is called Body of Light. With Conjunctional Correspondence 2 this can be done from a distance.<br /> I think that with Prime 2 a Mage should also be able to communicate through voice and/or sound as part of the Body of Light Effect. It can also be done with Forces 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-02-2018, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T03:57:55-07:00","id":1224128,"title":"","content":"Something worth noting; in order to directly alter the patterns of Garou, Fera, Fomori etc. (that is, living people who have a spiritual dimension directly tied onto them) a Mage does need to have Spirit. Any mage with Forces can launch a fireball at a Werewolf, but if you want to shapeshift it into something else, stop its heart, use it as the basis of a living Relic (a type of Wonder)... Spirit is a must.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T07:58:54-07:00","id":1224366,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna humbly suggest you ignore the M20 &quot;You need to know/use this skill to do matter magic&quot; thing. Because it's lore-breaking and kind of stupid.<br /> <br /> If I want to conjure some sort of magical sword out of thin air, I should not need to have to go through the rigamarole of actually crafting a sword. The 'Skill' Way of creating most things is just OoR/Technocracy Ritual that's been made coincidental enough that most people can use it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T08:08:36-07:00","id":1224367,"title":"","content":"have thought a time or two of the greedy mage wanting to suck up a caerns power. cliche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T10:07:48-07:00","id":1224386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage?p=1224366#post1224366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna humbly suggest you ignore the M20 &quot;You need to know/use this skill to do matter magic&quot; thing. Because it's lore-breaking and kind of stupid.<br /> <br /> If I want to conjure some sort of magical sword out of thin air, I should not need to have to go through the rigamarole of actually crafting a sword. The 'Skill' Way of creating most things is just OoR/Technocracy Ritual that's been made coincidental enough that most people can use it anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a few options here:<br /> <br /> - You need the relevant skills to create objects. Gunsmithing for a gun, Technology for a circuit, Smithing for a sword...<br /> <br /> - You need the relevant skills for complicated things, like creating a gun or a computer or a nuclear bomb, but not for simple things like a sword. Of course this has a huge problem... the person who is a master smith isn't allowed to conjure up a gun out of nowhere, since that's &quot;complicated&quot;, while a master gunsmith can conjure both a sword and a gun, since the sword is &quot;simple&quot;. But these Skills cost the same amount, and it just feels like a ruling which makes things harder on those with 'traditional' skills.<br /> <br /> - Anyone can do anything. Know what a gun is? Sure, mysteriously you can create all the components and put them in the right place without actually needing to understand how a gun works. It's simple to handwave this stuff, but it doesn't feel thematic. Mages are <i>excellent</i>. They are information hoarders who master skills and crafts and ideas. And Magick is thematically and mechanically powerful when it builds off of abilities.<br /> <br /> Personally I think that M20's approach is perfect. Regardless of whether you're a Mystic or a Technomancer, you need to have knowledge backing up your craft. Of course someone with Medicine 0 can create &quot;bandages&quot; with Matter, just as someone can grab a teatowel or tear a dress to make a bandage with no healthcare experience. It's just going to be a poor bandage, and they're not going to apply it well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 06-03-2018, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T12:52:19-07:00","id":1224418,"title":"","content":"... Except it's neither mechanically, nor thematically powerful.<br /> <br /> For example. Suppose you NEEDED to know Thermodynamics to use Forces. You had to get a bunch of successes to craft a fireball because you had to scientifically know how fire works. This would quite rightly be viewed as ridiculous. Or you had to know Psychology to perform Mind Effects, and needed to roll a bunch of successes. Ditto.<br /> <br /> It doesn't change just because the sphere is Matter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T13:32:43-07:00","id":1224424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage?p=1224418#post1224418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Except it's neither mechanically, nor thematically powerful.<br /> <br /> For example. Suppose you NEEDED to know Thermodynamics to use Forces. You had to get a bunch of successes to craft a fireball because you had to scientifically know how fire works. This would quite rightly be viewed as ridiculous. Or you had to know Psychology to perform Mind Effects, and needed to roll a bunch of successes. Ditto.<br /> <br /> It doesn't change just because the sphere is Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is apples and oranges.<br /> <br /> Moving fire around, as with Forces 2, is akin to making something melt, or changing its shape, which requires no specialist knowledge in and of itself. Anyone with Matter can bend a sword to make it useless, or punch through a concrete wall. Conjuring fire is akin to conjuring water or earth; this is literally as simple as it gets in terms of patterns.<br /> <br /> If someone wants to create a complex pattern with a Pattern Sphere, such as creating a mega AI with Mind 5, or creating a perfect blade with Prime and Matter, or creating a cyborg with Matter and Prime, then they need specialist knowledge (Computer, Swordsmithing and Biotech, respectively). M20 simply applies this logic to effects like creating guns and swords with Matter, or creating radiation with Forces. The idea is to make it so that there's a difference between a Matter/Forces specialist who is a spiritualist bound to a fire goddess, and a Matter/Forces specialist who is the master of radioactive materials. It's at the core of Mage honestly. It would just be hilariously stupid if a person could conjure up a weapon they don't understand, much as it would be ridiculous if they could make a cyborg with no points in Biotech.<br /> <br /> TECHNICALLY Matter/Life is all you need to bond extensive cybernetics (such as coating their bones with metal) to a person without rejection or side effects, but M20 has &quot;Do you even know what you're doing?!&quot; as a useful rule to stop the wicka priestess from installing cybernetic upgrades (I mean unless she's a technomystic wickapunk sorceress or something, but you get what I mean).<br /> <br /> To summarize...<br /> <br /> - You can do a tonne with Matter besides creating objects out of nothing, or from random junk.<br /> <br /> - If you want to create a pattern, you will often need to have some idea of what it is you're doing. This applies to all of the Pattern Spheres.<br /> <br /> - Do You Even Know What You're Doing?! applies to a lot of examples outside of doing stuff with Matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T07:05:24-07:00","id":1224671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage?p=1224424#post1224424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is apples and oranges.<br /> <br /> ...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The writing of M20 unequivocally states that you need to know how to make a computer to summon a working one on the grounds that a computer it's a complex pattern.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm sure you agree that the human body it's pretty damn complex (I would balk at any attempt at saying that regenerating leg or curing poison or a deadly virus it's somehow less complex that building or fixing a computer). So, since &quot;M20 approach it's perfect&quot;, would you say you need Medicine to heal someone <i>with Faith</i>?<br /> <br /> I suppose no...because &quot;this is apples and oranges&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now a Verbena needs Medicine to create a human body, because the human body it's damn complex - then how did ancient mages managed do so before our interpretation of Medicine was a thing?. Or must I believe that ancient mages hadn't the resources to create a human, in spite of countless legends that have mages building people from clay, within cauldrons, and such stuff? This rule flies in the face of Paradigms that don't believe that *they* are the ones doing the magic (i.e: A Chorsiter asking God for a computer - God doesn't know?) and also on the face of Paradigms that believe science it's not right.<br /> <br /> Hence, I heavily disagree in that &quot;M20's approach is perfect&quot;. M20 approach it's &quot;fixable&quot; if we allow to use alternate Skills (religion for faith healing?, Esoterica for beliefs that don't acknowledge modern biology?)<br /> <br /> However, I think that doing so it's the wrong approach to problem of &quot;Do You Even Know What You're Doing?!&quot; . As allways and ever, Satyros rules with no carrot and a lot of stick. A good roleplayer should build a mage with the skills relevant to their Craft, this kind of build should be <i>rewarded</i>.<br /> Instead M20 taxes everyone else's - and because Mage it's so vast it's no wonder that fringe innocent builds end being diminished too.Summoning the spirit of fire to blast someone?. OK. Summoning the spirit of money to get cash?. Bad. Now a mage can't put two dollar bills together and &quot;reproduce them&quot; using their mystical lore - nope, you need to know everything about money even when *you* aren't creating anything, but merely using a form of &quot;natural reproduction&quot; that should be as effective in building a complex object as any mother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-04-2018, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T07:44:18-07:00","id":1224682,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> M20 makes it clear that Esoterica: Traditional Healing can be used as a knowledge base for certain things, such as the basis for healing complex diseases with Chi (for example). Ancient Mages who wanted to create human beings &quot;out of thin air&quot; did so with detailed knowledge of the human body as understood by their paradigm.<br /> <br /> And it's not like Mages are Bereft of a way to investigate a Pattern. If you're trying to create a Pattern with Prime and a Pattern Sphere, you have Level 1 in that Pattern Sphere as a prerequisite. Ancient masters of Life will have analysed the human body with Life 1 until they understood it well enough to replicate it. The same applies to all of the Pattern Spheres, honestly. Every Mage has a great justification for learning all of the Abilities they need. Now an ST could choose to hand-wave the Abilities requirements by letting a level 1 effect analyse what you want to replicate to get sufficient information... and you know what, that works. But it still doesn't help a person who is attempting to create something out of nowhere without an example to analyse of course.<br /> <br /> The question of &quot;Do you even know what you're doing?&quot; is a *question* after all. All you need to be able to do is sincerely say &quot;yes, I absolutely do&quot; and point to some trait which would reasonably give you the necessary mental scaffolding. And that could be modern medicine, a thorough understanding of a traditional healing method, a specialisation of esoterica...<br /> <br /> As for money vs. fire, this is again apples vs. oranges. Money is intentionally difficult to reproduce and create, even moreso in the WoD with the Syndicate's involvement. Currency isn't easy to replicate. Fire is so easy to replicate that it does so when we don't want it to. Conjuring up a single coherent substance, like water or air or a type of metal is very different to pulling out a roll of 20s. This is a feature, not a bug, for the Technocracy. They have filled the world with things we are utterly dependent on, where you need to play *their* game to truly optimize their use with magick.<br /> <br /> &quot;But my mage believes that replicating something is simple-&quot; Well good for them. Maybe they think that their Box of Duplication rote will work for everything, up to and including a revolver, but you could just as easily claim that in *your* Mage's paradigm, the human body is just made up of Force and Matter patterns which interplay, so that means a Forces/Matter rote can easily end someone's life by stopping their heart, no Life needed. I could claim that my astrophysicist's paradigm draws no distinction between Correspondence/Forces and Time, since Time is continuous with Space and relies on Gravitational Force, so do I *really* have to invest in Time like everyone else? Mage needs to have concrete rules which will defy some ideas in certain magickal traditions. If you want to duplicate money easily, have counterfeiting or similar to give the knowledge base for Matter/Prime duplication. And if you want to pull a sword or a gun out of thin air, or create a sentient AI etc., it's the same deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 06-04-2018, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T14:22:29-07:00","id":1225082,"title":"","content":"Wow guys, thank you all, you have give me a lot to think and some cool ideas, I will try to clarify to some of your questions.<br /> (Sorry for the delay)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>menos125</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage?p=1223905#post1223905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, for you to understand the &quot;power level&quot; of mage you should take in consideration their Arete which is alone used on Magick rolls, however what truly defines what makes a character really powerfull isnt his &quot;magic muscle&quot;, but their Spheres dots, you see as you asked a character to be defined an Archmage must have on sphere in rank 6 - archmaestry. Even if you have a character with 6 or more arete it doest not count exactly as and archmage. But to define excessive strength you have to consider that mages are not battle oriented as werewolves are, and if they try do do so they may get underrated or absurdly overpower. Just an example: if Steve wants to throw a lighting bolt at &quot;pc 1&quot;, he rolls 3 successes, and he wants to put all those successes in damage, it will deal 2 damage per success and +1 for merely using Forces sphere, it will be in total 7 points of aggravated damage, because all damages done by Forces are naturally aggravated. Well Im happy for you that garou can soak agg, because if not, damn if it would be fatal damage done by a mere starting character with Forces 3 and Arete 3.<br /> However remember, what maks mages fking powerfull isnt Forces alone, but the absurd versatility those guys have, they can do EVERYTHING a garou and any other splat form world of darks can do, at the cost of paradox.<br /> <br /> <br /> They are quite possible and you dont need that much high ranks for such, you can do that about going in the umbra with Lvl 3, but to imprison spirits on objects against their will it needs to be 4, also about taking people here and there so easily also means 4, with this lvl you can rip the boundaries of the spirit and material world, literally opening a portal betwen the two. (knowing that how could malfean nephandi corrupted mages didnt just summon Wyrm on the fking world already is beyong me)</div> </div> </div> </div>Between this and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> answer I think I have a clear picture of the power levels and social implications, I think I will go with 4 dots in Spirit even if I have to dump other spheres to signal his obsession with that kind of knowledge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It depends of what you understand by wards, in mage terms is to completely negate or difficult usage of said routine or sphere in all of its regards. If you're talking about defending oneself about, lets say, Paw of the Newborn-bla-bla-overrated-gift, all you would probably need is Spirit, Prime or other spheres you think to be, by logic, part of the intended purpose, like healing with Life, mind control with Mind, etc. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage?p=1224080#post1224080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forces 2 can conjure forcefields, that may be all the ward you need. Unlike Correspondence Wards, enough brute force should be able to overpower a forcefield.<br /> In M20 you need Matter 2 if you want to put a forcefiled in a building or another material object without concentrating on the spell, if you don't want to use this whole &quot;pattern locking&quot; rules fell free to house-rule them away, nothing breaks.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think Forces is the one I was looking for, maybe with Spirit for warding the Umbra too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dont know, what ends you think you will get by using it, makes people a bit spirit? Makes them easier to be snatched into another dimension? You only use a Sphere if the Effect has parts of it directly related to the sphere usage, as much as the teleport example. Using blood makes a lot of sense, but we have to understand what exactly you want it to be used for. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want it to have a magical effect, you're probably thinking in Prime. Prime 3 can enchant a substane into a consumables that causes magical effects, called Charms. Prime 2 it's enough if you use Tass with a ressonance appropiate to the spell the object it's going to cast - which you could rule kinfolk blood it's (this would be a house rule - kinfolk usually don't count as magical creatures, albeit kinfolk with Gnosis could be the exception). Note that the mage needs to be able to cast the spell he's imbuing into the charm. </div> </div> </div>He produces a drug that allow people to see faintly thought the Gauntlet, people just assume it is a really cool high, every use thins the gauntlet ver so slightly.<br /> So Spirit + Prime looks appropriate here, right?<br /> <br /> The projection power can be done in several ways, that's nice.<br /> <br /> I may ditch the secret door spell given what you tell me.<br /> <br /> And I think I get the picture with the Sanctum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage?p=1224128#post1224128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something worth noting; in order to directly alter the patterns of Garou, Fera, Fomori etc. (that is, living people who have a spiritual dimension directly tied onto them) a Mage does need to have Spirit. Any mage with Forces can launch a fireball at a Werewolf, but if you want to shapeshift it into something else, stop its heart, use it as the basis of a living Relic (a type of Wonder)... Spirit is a must.</div> </div> </div> </div>This gives me two questions, a spell to revert the Garou to their breed form would be spirit + life, right? <br /> And although Gnosis and Quintessenceis not the same, thematically makes sense to be able to siphon the spiritual power (Gnosis) from the Garou to the Mage(Quintessence), Spirit + Prime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":20067,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20067-hares666","user":"Hares666","date":". 06-05-2018, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20067-hares666","name":"Hares666","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20067_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T14:28:01-07:00","id":1225084,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20067-hares666\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar20067_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"20067\" data-vbnamecard=\"20067\">Hares666</a> yes some simple Spirit 1 + Prime 2 would even do that. Prime 2 to make Charms, Spirit 1 to give perception through the Gauntlet. It isn't necessary to thin the gauntlet, just to allow someone to peek through it after all. And it's Coincidental thanks to them being mixed with hallucinogens of course!<br /> <br /> Another thing worth keeping in mind is a Spiritual Foundation. Using Life, Prime and Forces a Mage can &quot;charm&quot; a fox to be immune to heat and fire, and create small fires with ashen coughs. This is a living foundation. A spiritual foundation requires Spirit and Prime, and lets you expand upon a spirit's abilities. To many Spirits and Mages this is a really taboo thing. Spirits simply Are. They are extra Real, and they don't change. They might embody Change, but they are what they are. Modifying them with mortal magick is usually held in poor regard. But with particularly corrupted spirits, and a Mage who lacks such reservations (this doesn't necessary make them evil!), you can end up with mega-banes who can set things on fire without spending their Essence, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T14:30:37-07:00","id":1225085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage?p=1224049#post1224049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theme question: Vodou is already syncretized with Christianity. Is this just a case where there's an extra helping of Christianity?<br /> <br /> Mages can easily have non-magical cohorts such as a family, congregation, civic group, community and such that can fill in whatever holes you encounter. This also allows the Mage to have more firepower of whatever type you need without throwing in an extra dot. Mages also have access to chiminage to barter with spirits and, if doing work with Vodou, maybe even the undead so you have a lot of knobs to work with. Whether your character is a Houngan, a Mambo, or bokor, you have a lot of options for invoking powers from any of the main families augmented with the Christian saints either as a focus or through their spirit agents.<br /> <br /> Also, when you're throwing in another system, there's nothing to say can't just have a list of vague powers that you want to work with. The full system for Wraith is a bit daunting but thumbing through Arcanos gives you ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage?p=1224080#post1224080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you want to research about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santer%C3%ADa\" target=\"_blank\">Santeria</a>...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I did know about some of this but I didn't remember the santeria stuff and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar15603_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"15603\" data-vbnamecard=\"15603\">PhillyCuriosity</a> those names look like a nice evening of research, thank you!<br /> <br /> I am not going to enter into the Expert vs Intuitive debate because you are the experts but in this particular case my mage has chemists in his payroll that produce the actual drug he then adds the final touches.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20067-hares666","name":"Hares666","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20067_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T07:58:40-07:00","id":1225273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1223891-creating-an-antagonistic-mage?p=1225082#post1225082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This gives me two questions, a spell to revert the Garou to their breed form would be spirit + life, right?<br /> And although Gnosis and Quintessenceis not the same, thematically makes sense to be able to siphon the spiritual power (Gnosis) from the Garou to the Mage(Quintessence), Spirit + Prime?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I wasn't the one that provided that piece of insight, yes, that's exact.<br /> <br /> Prime 3 it's used to suck Quint, the level of Spirit needed to share the love with Gnosis aren't clear but 3 it's a reasonable choice (when in doubt, use the same levels of both Spheres)<br /> <br /> There was a Rote to revert shapeshifters to their breed form (and keep them there for a few rounds) and it was Spirit + Life, but I don't remember the levels. <br /> <br /> Shapeshifting people it's a hard thing - you need Life 5 to transform a human into a pig, for instance. Now, I'm sure the Rote wasn't THAT expensive. From a metaphysical standpoint, a lower requisite can be justified by saying you're just manipulating the natural ability of Garou to shapeshifts, a lvl 4 should be enough to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T01:42:38-07:00","id":1225831,"title":"","content":"For Sphere levels, your Vodoun would need Spirit 4, Correspondence 4, Forces 3, and Prime 3 to accomplish all you want him to do.<br /> <br /> To add to that, I would recommend that &quot;Steve&quot; also have Life 3. This would allow him to heal his wounds (or the wounds of others), perform countermagic to negate shifting into different forms, soak Aggravated damage, give himself natural weapons like claws (which, with Prime 3, can be made to deal Aggravated damage), and to (with Spirit 2) do direct Aggravated damage to a werewolf's Pattern. For anyone looking to tangle with shifters, these abilities are invaluable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}